# Sensitive paths for shipping-work-python-fastapi's Step 1.5 doc check.
#
# Replaces doc-check.sh's built-in FastAPI defaults wholesale — it does not
# extend them, so a default added upstream has to be added here too. Entries
# match whole path SEGMENTS at any depth: `pyproject.toml` covers the root
# file and `clients/python/pyproject.toml`, `deploy/` covers `tests/deploy/`.
#
# Dropped from the defaults, all three dead in this tree:
#   schema.sql      — schema is Alembic's, never raw SQL
#   src/models/     — models live in src/core/, under src/core/ below
#   .env.example    — none tracked; env vars are documented in AGENTS.md
# Added beyond them, each a surface the docs describe in enough detail to rot:
#   scripts/            — AGENTS.md's Common Commands and Server Lifecycle
#   .github/workflows/  — AGENTS.md's Continuous Integration section
#   skills/             — the docs/SKILLS.md inventory and its vendor pins
#   skills-vendor/      — a submodule bump arrives as this one gitlink path and
#                         is what silently stales an override's SKILL.md (#47)
#   .skills/            — this file's own policy, mirrored in docs/SKILLS.md
#                         and docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
#
# tests/ci/test_doc_sensitive_paths.py fails on an entry that matches nothing.

AGENTS.md
README.md
CHANGELOG.md
pyproject.toml
uv.lock
alembic/versions/
deploy/
src/api/
src/core/
scripts/
.github/workflows/
skills/
skills-vendor/
.skills/
